    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: xen: AMD Zen 2 Processors: Privilege escalation via improper CPU cache isolation (CVE-2025-54518)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Kernel crash in bpf_for_each_array_elem() due to missing backport of upstream commit 4b6313cf99b0 (JIRA:RHEL-191844)\n\n* gfs2: xfstests generic/363 failure [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:RHEL-214099)\n\n* RHEL8: HYPERV hv_storvsc driver can we add additional code to allow PERSISTENT_RESERVE_IN [RHEL 8.10Z]  (JIRA:RHEL-188270)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
